Third-party components

oonfeeWRT incorporates the Go runtime and standard library, third-party Go
packages, third-party JavaScript packages in its embedded production UI, and
Alpine's Mozilla-derived CA certificate bundle. The exact shipped versions,
provenance, copyright notices, and license texts are generated from pinned or
locked source material. The source-tree record is
third_party/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES; release archives and container images package
it as THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

The project orbit mark adapts the Lucide Orbit icon, copyright 2026 Lucide
Icons and Contributors, under the ISC License. Its source and full license
are retained in third_party/lucide-orbit and included in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.
This is a nonexclusive icon-based mark, not original or exclusive artwork.

Nothing in this repository is copied from OpenWrt, LuCI, or any vendor
firmware. Where the documentation quotes ACL fragments or ubus method names,
those are interface facts about the system being managed — the shape of an API
we call — not copied implementation.
